# Roblox Luau conventions

Apply to every Luau script you write, whether as a file (Rojo) or into Studio via MCP.

## Language
- Start every script with `--!strict`. Type function parameters/returns and module
  exports (`export type`). Use `unknown` for untrusted input (remote args) and narrow with
  `typeof`.
- Prefer `local` everything; no globals. Constants `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`, locals/functions
  `camelCase`, modules/classes/instances `PascalCase`.
- Use generalized iteration (`for k, v in t do`) instead of `pairs/ipairs` in new code.
- String interpolation with backticks: `` `Coins: {coins}` ``.
- Compound assignment (`+=`), `if x then a else b` expressions, `table.clone`,
  `table.freeze` for config tables.
- Never use `loadstring`, `getfenv`/`setfenv`, or `wait()`/`spawn()`/`delay()` - use
  `task.wait`, `task.spawn`, `task.defer`, `task.delay`.

## Roblox APIs
- Get services once at the top: `local Players = game:GetService("Players")`.
- `WaitForChild` with a timeout on the client for things the server creates; never on the
  server for things the server itself creates (create them first).
- Use `Instance.new(className)` then set properties, then set `Parent` **last**.
- Use `CollectionService` tags + `GetInstanceAddedSignal` for gameplay objects; Attributes
  for simple per-instance replicated state.
- Disconnect connections you own; clean up per-player state on `PlayerRemoving`.
- Prefer `TweenService` for UI/props motion; `RunService.Heartbeat` only for real per-frame
  work, never with yields inside.
- `pcall` every yielding network call: DataStores, MessagingService, HttpService,
  MarketplaceService, TeleportService. Retry with backoff.

## Structure
- One server entry `ServerScriptService.Server.Main` (Script) and one client entry
  `StarterPlayerScripts.ClientMain` (LocalScript); everything else is ModuleScripts with
  `start()` and no side effects at require time.
- Shared code in `ReplicatedStorage.Shared`; server-only code/assets in
  `ServerScriptService` / `ServerStorage`.
- Tunables in `ReplicatedStorage.Shared.Config`; no magic numbers in services.

## Networking and security
- Server is authoritative for anything valuable (currency, inventory, damage, progress).
- Every `OnServerEvent`: rate limit, type-check all args, range-check numbers (reject NaN/inf),
  length-check strings, verify ownership/distance, then act. Ignore invalid requests
  silently (optionally log).
- Server->client is RemoteEvent only; never `InvokeClient`.
- Never place secrets, admin lists, or anti-cheat logic where clients can read it.

## Style
- Tabs for indentation (StyLua defaults), max ~100 columns.
- Short header comment on each module: purpose and location.
- Comments explain *why*, not *what*.
